WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.135
Lesson 2.1.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.290
DEXs, aggregators & routing.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.319
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:08.622
able to choose where to swap by comparing

00:00:08.622 --> 00:00:11.145
the net amount received, not the quoted price.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.735
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.735 --> 00:00:15.420
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.135
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:19.660
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.822
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:26.539
What you actually get = quoted output −

00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:29.487
price impact − pool fees − gas.

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:33.016
First, AMM DEX: you trade against a liquidity

00:00:33.016 --> 00:00:36.232
pool priced by a formula (Lesson 2.2).

00:00:36.232 --> 00:00:39.128
Next, On-chain order book: orders matched by

00:00:39.128 --> 00:00:42.067
price and time, fully or partly on-chain.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:45.040
Then, Aggregator: searches many pools and venues

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.707
and may split your order across routes.

00:00:47.707 --> 00:00:49.541
Also, Price impact: how much

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:51.548
your trade moves the price.

00:00:51.548 --> 00:00:54.338
It grows with size relative to pool depth.

00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:56.996
On top of that, Slippage tolerance: the worst

00:00:56.996 --> 00:00:59.943
price you'll accept before the transaction reverts.

00:01:01.243 --> 00:01:04.094
And finally, Routing: multi-hop routes (A →

00:01:04.094 --> 00:01:05.714
B → C) can give a better

00:01:05.714 --> 00:01:07.723
price but touch more contracts.

00:01:09.023 --> 00:01:14.303
Selling 20 ETH: The aggregator wins by ~$308.

00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:18.084
Now selling 0.5 ETH: the aggregator quotes

00:01:18.084 --> 00:01:20.898
$3 better but costs $12 more in

00:01:20.898 --> 00:01:23.748
gas, so the direct pool wins.

00:01:23.748 --> 00:01:25.903
Big trades benefit from routing.

00:01:25.903 --> 00:01:28.193
Small trades mostly lose to gas.

00:01:28.193 --> 00:01:35.798
Single pool direct, 59,100 USDC, $8, 59,092.

00:01:35.798 --> 00:01:44.968
Aggregator (split across 3 pools), 59,420 USDC, $20, 59,400.

00:01:46.268 --> 00:01:47.728
Here's your checklist.

00:01:47.728 --> 00:01:49.263
Do it now, for real.

00:01:49.263 --> 00:01:53.238
First, Compare net output after gas, not headline price.

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:57.032
Next, Price impact shown and acceptable for the size.

00:01:57.032 --> 00:02:01.377
Then, Route uses reputable pools and tokens you've verified.

00:02:01.377 --> 00:02:04.732
And finally, Slippage set on purpose (see 2.5).

00:02:06.032 --> 00:02:07.242
Question 1.

00:02:07.242 --> 00:02:09.424
Why can an aggregator give a better price?

00:02:13.844 --> 00:02:16.389
The answer: It can split an order across

00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:18.809
pools, so each pool's price moves less.

00:02:20.109 --> 00:02:21.354
Question 2.

00:02:21.354 --> 00:02:22.899
When does the best quote lose?

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:30.064
The answer: When the extra gas costs more than

00:02:30.064 --> 00:02:33.335
the price improvement, which is common for small trades.

00:02:34.635 --> 00:02:35.905
Question 3.

00:02:35.905 --> 00:02:37.500
What drives price impact?

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.020
The answer: Trade size relative to pool liquidity.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.565
Let's recap.

00:02:47.565 --> 00:02:50.591
AMM DEX: you trade against a liquidity

00:02:50.591 --> 00:02:53.840
pool priced by a formula (Lesson 2.2).

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.703
On-chain order book: orders matched by price

00:02:56.703 --> 00:02:59.230
and time, fully or partly on-chain.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:02.004
Aggregator: searches many pools and venues and

00:03:02.004 --> 00:03:04.370
may split your order across routes.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:07.352
Price impact: how much your trade moves the price.

00:03:08.652 --> 00:03:11.167
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:15.248
Next up, Lesson 2.2: AMM Mathematics

00:03:15.248 --> 00:03:16.572
(x · y = k).
